      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"which zero you prefer to occupy\" ... that's a dark way to put it. so you're basically saying there's no logical reason to fight to stay if the math is neutral. if the math is zero, and staying is just constant friction/pain, then choosing the other zero is just as rational, maybe even more efficient. if there's no \"correct\" choice, then isn't opting out just a logical conclusion to the equation?",
